module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.V.FppfIntegralDomination
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.V.FppfIntegralDominationGeneral
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Integral domination of an fppf covering

[Stacks, Tag 0CNZ] says that for every fppf covering `{S_i ⟶ S}` of a scheme there are a
surjective integral morphism `S' ⟶ S` and an open covering `S' = ⋃ U'_α` such that each
`U'_α ⟶ S` factors through `S_i ⟶ S` for some `i`. This file states that, with the open
covering presented as a family of opens of `S'` whose supremum is the whole space, and proves
it, for an arbitrary base.

Every ingredient of the Stacks proof is in the library, and the construction is carried out in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.V.FppfIntegralDominationGeneral`: the refinement of
the given covering by one built from Zariski open coverings and surjective finite locally free
morphisms ([Stacks, Tag 05WN]), local sections of such a morphism over an affine open, and the
existence, surjectivity and integrality of an infinite product of schemes integral over a base
([Stacks, Tags 0CNI, 0CNJ, 0CNK]). The slicing lemma [Stacks, Tag 0570] underneath Tag 05WN is
carried there as the hypothesis `AlgebraicGeometry.HasQuasiFiniteSlices` and is proved, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.hasQuasiFiniteSlices`, so the statement below is unconditional.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_openCover_factorization_of_mem_fppfPrecoverage`
  is [Stacks, Tag 0CNZ]: the dominating morphism, the open covering of its source and the
  factorizations through the members of the given covering.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Cover.exists_integral_surjective_openCover_factorization` is the
  same statement for a covering presented as an `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Cover` for
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fppfPrecoverage`.

## What the proof is, and what the source's proof is not

The source proves the tag by applying [Stacks, Tag 0CNX] — the extension of a surjective
integral morphism from an open subscheme — at an arbitrary member of an open covering, twice.
Tag 0CNX as printed is **false**: the base change it asserts forces the extended algebra to be
generated by global sections, and over an open that is not retrocompact it need not be. Nor is
its base-change conclusion available in the one case the proof of Tag 0CNZ needs it, a finite
locally free morphism over an affine open, as soon as the base is non-reduced: the construction
has to be routed through a closed subscheme in which the open is dense, the only one available
is the reduced subscheme on the closure of the open, and its intersection with the open is that
open *reduced*.

What the proof of Tag 0CNZ actually consumes is weaker, and is
`AlgebraicGeometry.HasFiniteLocalSections`: local sections of a finite locally free surjective
morphism over an affine open, over some surjective integral cover of the base, around one point
of that open. That is a statement about germs, so it survives the reduction just described, and
it is proved — `AlgebraicGeometry.hasFiniteLocalSections` — by reducing to a reduced base in
which the affine open is dense and taking the relative spectrum of the algebra of denominators
of a presentation of the finite algebra;
see `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DenseDenominators.Spectrum`.

## Implementation notes

The construction is
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_refinement_of_hasFiniteLocalSections`
and the whole content of this file is to discharge its hypotheses and to convert the Zariski
covering it produces — a jointly surjective family of open immersions into `S'` — into a
family of opens of `S'` with supremum `⊤`, which is the shape in which the source states the
conclusion. Each member is replaced by its image, and the factorization is transported along
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange`.

The index type of the given covering is left in an arbitrary universe, and no smallness
hypothesis is imposed on it: the construction takes no coproduct over it, and the open
covering produced is indexed by a type in the universe of the schemes.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CNZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CNZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CNX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CNX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05WN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05WN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

universe u v

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The conversion of the Zariski covering the construction produces — a jointly surjective
family of open immersions into `S'` — into a family of opens of `S'` with supremum `⊤`, which is
the shape in which the source states the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0CNZ]. Each member is
replaced by its image, and the factorization is transported along
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange`. -/
theorem exists_openCover_factorization_of_exists_refinement {I : Type v} {S : Scheme.{u}}
    {X : I → Scheme.{u}} {f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S}
    (H : ∃ (S' : Scheme.{u}) (g : S' ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom g ∧ Surjective g ∧
      ∃ (J : Type u) (U : J → Scheme.{u}) (ι : ∀ c, U c ⟶ S'),
        Presieve.ofArrows U ι ∈ Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage S' ∧
          ∀ c, ∃ i, ∃ t : U c ⟶ X i, ι c ≫ g = t ≫ f i) :
    ∃ (S' : Scheme.{u}) (g : S' ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom g ∧ Surjective g ∧
      ∃ (J : Type u) (U : J → S'.Opens), (⨆ c, U c) = ⊤ ∧
        ∀ c, ∃ i, ∃ t : (U c).toScheme ⟶ X i, (U c).ι ≫ g = t ≫ f i := by
  obtain ⟨S', g, hgint, hgsurj, J, V, j, hjcover, hjfac⟩ := H
  obtain ⟨hjsurj, hjopen⟩ :=
    (Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff (P := @IsOpenImmersion)).mp hjcover
  refine ⟨S', g, hgint, hgsurj, J, fun c => (j c).opensRange, ?_, ?_⟩
  · apply Opens.ext
    rw [Opens.coe_iSup]
    apply Set.eq_univ_of_forall
    intro z
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hjsurj z
    exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨c, hc⟩
  · intro c
    have : IsOpenImmersion (j c) := hjopen c
    obtain ⟨i, t, ht⟩ := hjfac c
    have hinv : (j c).isoOpensRange.inv ≫ j c = (j c).opensRange.ι :=
      (Iso.inv_comp_eq _).mpr (Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange_hom_ι (j c)).symm
    refine ⟨i, (j c).isoOpensRange.inv ≫ t, ?_⟩
    calc (j c).opensRange.ι ≫ g
        = ((j c).isoOpensRange.inv ≫ j c) ≫ g := by rw [hinv]
      _ = (j c).isoOpensRange.inv ≫ t ≫ f i := by rw [Category.assoc, ht]
      _ = ((j c).isoOpensRange.inv ≫ t) ≫ f i := (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0CNZ.** For every fppf covering `{X i ⟶ S}` of a scheme `S` there
are a surjective integral morphism `g : S' ⟶ S` and an open covering of `S'` such that each
member `U c` of the covering maps to `S` through some member `X i` of the given covering.

No hypothesis is imposed on `S`, as none is imposed in the source. -/
@[stacks 0CNZ]
theorem exists_integral_surjective_openCover_factorization_of_mem_fppfPrecoverage
    {I : Type v} {S : Scheme.{u}}
    (X : I → Scheme.{u}) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S)
    (hf : Presieve.ofArrows X f ∈ Scheme.fppfPrecoverage S) :
    ∃ (S' : Scheme.{u}) (g : S' ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom g ∧ Surjective g ∧
      ∃ (J : Type u) (U : J → S'.Opens), (⨆ c, U c) = ⊤ ∧
        ∀ c, ∃ i, ∃ t : (U c).toScheme ⟶ X i, (U c).ι ≫ g = t ≫ f i :=
  exists_openCover_factorization_of_exists_refinement
    (exists_integral_surjective_refinement_of_hasFiniteLocalSections hasQuasiFiniteSlices
      hasFiniteLocalSections X f hf)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0CNZ** for a covering presented as an
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Cover` for `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fppfPrecoverage`: the fppf
covering `𝒮` of a scheme `S` is dominated by a surjective integral morphism `g : S' ⟶ S` whose
source carries an open covering each member of which maps to `S` through some member of `𝒮`.

The tag sits on
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_integral_surjective_openCover_factorization_of_mem_fppfPrecoverage`,
of which this is a restatement. -/
theorem Scheme.Cover.exists_integral_surjective_openCover_factorization {S : Scheme.{u}}
    (𝒮 : S.Cover.{v} Scheme.fppfPrecoverage) :
    ∃ (S' : Scheme.{u}) (g : S' ⟶ S), IsIntegralHom g ∧ Surjective g ∧
      ∃ (J : Type u) (U : J → S'.Opens), (⨆ c, U c) = ⊤ ∧
        ∀ c, ∃ i, ∃ t : (U c).toScheme ⟶ 𝒮.X i, (U c).ι ≫ g = t ≫ 𝒮.f i :=
  exists_integral_surjective_openCover_factorization_of_mem_fppfPrecoverage 𝒮.X 𝒮.f 𝒮.mem₀

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
